From: leopard-webkit-build
Subject: [PATCH] OptionsMac: register ENABLE_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT_GL + include GStreamerDefinitions

Two related wiring bugs in OptionsMac.cmake were silently forcing
USE_GSTREAMER_GL OFF at compile time, defeating the entire GL video sink
build path despite find_package(GStreamer 1.4.5 ... gl) succeeding,
PC_GSTREAMER_GL_FOUND=1, and libgstgl-1.0.dylib being located.

Bug 1: ENABLE_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT_GL was registered as a WEBKIT_OPTION only
in OptionsGTK.cmake:92 and OptionsWPE.cmake:89. OptionsMac.cmake:120
used plain set() which is invisible to the WEBKIT_OPTION framework.

Bug 2 (the deeper one): GStreamerDefinitions.cmake — which holds
WEBKIT_OPTION_DEFINE(USE_GSTREAMER_GL ...) — was included from
OptionsGTK.cmake:58 and OptionsWPE.cmake:40 but NOT from OptionsMac.
So USE_GSTREAMER_GL was never registered as a WEBKIT_OPTION on Mac at
all; the dependency check in GStreamerDependencies.cmake:2 never fired
because the dependent option didn't exist.

Consequence: every #if USE(GSTREAMER_GL) source guard evaluated false.
GLVideoSinkGStreamer.cpp's body compiled to an empty translation unit.
PlatformDisplayGStreamer.cpp wasn't added to the build at all. The
patched libgstgl + libgstopengl.so deployed to the bundle had no
WebCore consumer.

Verification that the fix takes: DUSE_GSTREAMER_GL=1 must appear in
every WebCore gstreamer TU's compile command post-rebuild. Previously
absent.

Both changes must be inside WEBKIT_OPTION_BEGIN/END scope (per
WebKitFeatures.cmake:14 guard).

See spikes/gstreamer-webkit-header-floor/README.md HEADLINE FINDING.

---
diff --git a/Source/cmake/OptionsMac.cmake b/Source/cmake/OptionsMac.cmake
--- a/Source/cmake/OptionsMac.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/OptionsMac.cmake
@@ -110,6 +110,15 @@
 WEBKIT_OPTION_DEFAULT_PORT_VALUE(ENABLE_WIRELESS_PLAYBACK_TARGET PRIVATE OFF) # [leopard] OFF to match ENABLE_VIDEO=OFF (avoids dangling RemotePlayback vtable)
 WEBKIT_OPTION_DEFAULT_PORT_VALUE(ENABLE_XSLT PRIVATE ON)

+# [leopard] Register ENABLE_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT_GL as a WEBKIT_OPTION AND pull
+# in GStreamerDefinitions.cmake (which holds WEBKIT_OPTION_DEFINE(USE_GSTREAMER_GL ...)).
+# Without both, USE_GSTREAMER_GL stays unregistered on Mac and every
+# #if USE(GSTREAMER_GL) source guard evaluates false at compile time,
+# silently disabling the entire GL video sink code path.
+# Matches OptionsGTK.cmake:58 + :92 / OptionsWPE.cmake:40 patterns.
+include(GStreamerDefinitions)
+WEBKIT_OPTION_DEFINE(ENABLE_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT_GL "Whether to use OpenGL." PUBLIC ON)
+
 WEBKIT_OPTION_END()

 # [leopard] Enable GStreamer media backend for 10.6 (replaces AVFoundation which is 10.7+).
